        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<picture><source media="(min-width: 1120px)" srcset="https://assets-eu-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/ef593040-b591-0198-9506-ed88b30bc023/53fb6dd6-5c86-41da-9e04-0c9b450af211/content_527_code_quality_security_blog_index_2x.webp?w=352&amp;h=217&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=70 1x, https://assets-eu-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/ef593040-b591-0198-9506-ed88b30bc023/53fb6dd6-5c86-41da-9e04-0c9b450af211/content_527_code_quality_security_blog_index_2x.webp?w=352&amp;h=217&amp;dpr=2&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=70 2x" width="352" height="217"><source media="(min-width: 720px)" srcset="https://assets-eu-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/ef593040-b591-0198-9506-ed88b30bc023/53fb6dd6-5c86-41da-9e04-0c9b450af211/content_527_code_quality_security_blog_index_2x.webp?w=720&amp;h=443&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=70 1x, https://assets-eu-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/ef593040-b591-0198-9506-ed88b30bc023/53fb6dd6-5c86-41da-9e04-0c9b450af211/content_527_code_quality_security_blog_index_2x.webp?w=720&amp;h=443&amp;dpr=2&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=70 2x" width="720" height="443"><source srcset="https://assets-eu-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/ef593040-b591-0198-9506-ed88b30bc023/53fb6dd6-5c86-41da-9e04-0c9b450af211/content_527_code_quality_security_blog_index_2x.webp?w=500&amp;h=307.69&amp;dpr=1&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=70 1x, https://assets-eu-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/ef593040-b591-0198-9506-ed88b30bc023/53fb6dd6-5c86-41da-9e04-0c9b450af211/content_527_code_quality_security_blog_index_2x.webp?w=500&amp;h=307.69&amp;dpr=2&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=70 2x" width="500" height="307.69"><img src="https://assets-eu-01.kc-usercontent.com:443/ef593040-b591-0198-9506-ed88b30bc023/53fb6dd6-5c86-41da-9e04-0c9b450af211/content_527_code_quality_security_blog_index_2x.webp?w=500&amp;h=307.69&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=70" class="css-nm7ja6 e1yv2nyc2" alt="Image for Why prioritizing code quality is the fastest way to reduce&nbsp;security risks" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="500" height="307.69"></picture><div class="css-o76qu6 e1yv2nyc3"><span class="css-4tlw9v e1yv2nyc8">Blog post</span><h3 class="css-fjv57c e1yv2nyc6">Why prioritizing code quality is the fastest way to reduce&nbsp;security risks</h3><p class="css-vunwgt e1yv2nyc5">The common perception is that a security vulnerability is a rare, complex attack pattern. In reality, the journey of most flaws begins much earlier and much more simply: as a&nbsp;code quality&nbsp;issue. For both developers and security practitioners, understanding this lifecycle is crucial to building secure, reliable, and maintainable software. </p><p class="css-18j4al9 e1yv2nyc4">Read article &gt;</p></div>]]></content>
